# NLP Service (Python / SpaCy)

## Available endpoints

| Endpoint | Input | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| `POST /analyze` | `{ text: string }` | tokens with POS, lemma, dep, morph |
| `POST /check-dehet` | `{ nouns: string[] }` | `{ word, prediction, confidence }[]` |
| `POST /lemmatize` | `{ words: string[] }` | `{ word, lemma, pos }[]` |
| `GET /health` | — | `{ status: "ok" }` |

## Calling from Next.js (use the lib wrapper, not fetch directly)

```ts
import { nlp } from '@/lib/nlp'

const analysis = await nlp.analyze('Ik bel je morgen op')
// analysis.tokens[].pos — VERB, NOUN, ADP, etc.
// analysis.tokens[].dep — nsubj, obj, advmod, etc.
// analysis.tokens[].lemma — base form
```

## Adding a new endpoint to the service

1. Add Pydantic model for request/response in `services/nlp/main.py`
2. Add the route function
3. Add the corresponding method to `apps/web/src/lib/nlp.ts`
4. Update `services/nlp/Dockerfile` only if new packages are needed

## Dutch POS tags to know

`NOUN` `VERB` `AUX` `ADJ` `ADV` `ADP` `CCONJ` `SCONJ` `DET` `PRON` `PROPN`

Separable verb detection: look for `VERB + PART` dependency pair.
